Kernir patch 0025: the seekable zip reader charges the central-directory comments it keeps to the names total

Upstream: libarchive 3.8.10, libarchive/archive_read_support_format_zip.c (slurp_central_directory),
include/kernir_names.h (its comment). Applies on top of 0001-0024 (0012 and 0022 lines included).

Patch 0012 keeps every central-directory record's comment (up to 65,535 bytes each) in its zip_entry until the reader
is freed, and slurp_central_directory reads the whole central directory before the first header, so a crafted zip of
records with long comments had libarchive hold about its own size in comment bytes (a 1 GB zip, 1 GB), outside
patch 0022's limits, whatever the caller's names total (Quick Look's preview: 64 MiB). Only the seekable zip reader
keeps per-entry comments: the streaming zip reader skips them, and no other reader keeps one per entry.

Each record's comment is now charged to 0022's names counter after its name, before it is copied, against the same
allowance, max(names_bytes, name_bytes_per_entry × the listed records so far) (__archive_read_kernir_names_allowance);
names plus comments over it are refused (ARCHIVE_FATAL, ARCHIVE_ERRNO_FILE_FORMAT, own message, "ZIP entry comments
take the entry names past the names limit", which Kernir maps to its names limit). No new limit: the comments are
held to what the names may take, so the reader holds at most the names total in names and comments together. The
archive is refused rather than read without its comments: Kernir lists no entry comment, but a zip -> zip save copies
them, and a save that dropped them would lose them silently; an honest zip with more than 64 MiB (preview) or
256 MiB of entry comments is not known. Records whose local header offset repeats keep their comment too, so they are
charged too. Archives within the limits read as before.

Apply from Sources/CLibArchive: patch -p1 < patches/0025-zip-comments-names-total.patch

--- a/include/kernir_names.h
+++ b/include/kernir_names.h
@@ -55,7 +55,8 @@
      entry, whatever numFiles claims: the block is allocated before any entry is parsed.
    Patch 0022: the seekable zip reader holds its central-directory records to max_entries (records with a new local
    header offset: the headers it returns) and 2 × max_entries (every record, saturated, before it is allocated), and
-   the record names to max(names_bytes, name_bytes_per_entry × the listed records so far).
+   the record names to max(names_bytes, name_bytes_per_entry × the listed records so far). Patch 0025: the record
+   comments it keeps (patch 0012) are charged to that names total too, before they are copied.
    The defaults below are NestingLimits.standard's (maxEntries, maxTotalNameBytes, nameBytesPerEntry), which a
    test checks. Set before archive_read_open; ARCHIVE_OK then. A call after it returns ARCHIVE_FATAL and also puts
    the handle itself in ARCHIVE_STATE_FATAL (archive_check_magic), so the open read fails from then on; only
--- a/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_zip.c
+++ b/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_zip.c
@@ -4649,10 +4649,14 @@
 		 * order. So a crafted central directory whose long names come
 		 * before the records that grow the allowance (or whose names
 		 * are longer than the local headers') can be refused here
-		 * though Kernir would take the headers. Names within
-		 * names_bytes are never refused, and a central directory in
-		 * offset order, with no repeated offset and the local headers'
-		 * names, only where Kernir refuses its headers too. */
+		 * though Kernir would take the headers. Names and comments
+		 * (patch 0025) within names_bytes are never refused, and a
+		 * central directory in offset order, with no repeated offset
+		 * and the local headers' names, only where Kernir refuses its
+		 * headers too. The comments count too (patch 0025), so when
+		 * earlier comments use up the allowance, the next record's
+		 * name is refused with the names message below; the Swift
+		 * error is the same .totalPathBytes. */
 		if (kernir_listed > a->kernir_max_entries)
 			return (kernir_zip_refuse(a,
 			    "ZIP archive has more entries than the entry limit"));
@@ -4664,6 +4668,17 @@
 
 		/* Kernir patch 0012: keep the comment bytes. */
 		if (comment_length > 0) {
+			/* Kernir patch 0025: they are kept for every record
+			 * until the reader is freed (up to 65535 bytes each,
+			 * about the central directory's size in all), so they
+			 * are charged to the names total with the names,
+			 * before they are copied. */
+			kernir_names += comment_length;
+			if (kernir_names > __archive_read_kernir_names_allowance(
+			    a, kernir_listed))
+				return (kernir_zip_refuse(a,
+				    "ZIP entry comments take the entry names "
+				    "past the names limit"));
 			p = __archive_read_ahead(a,
 			    filename_length + extra_length + comment_length,
 			    NULL);
